Jump and links
The first slot of Jump is not a number field but a [b]target button[/b] (the button shows which block it is locked to):

[ul]
[*]Press and hold on the button, drag onto a block and release = lock the jump to that block;
[*]Release on itself or on the block list on the left = unlock;
[*]Release on empty space / right-click / Esc = cancel and leave it as it was.
[/ul]

Once locked, a [b]link line[/b] appears on the canvas: it runs out of the left side of the Jump and over to the target block, colored per target,
and overlapping lines are automatically staggered into layers. While dragging, the candidate block under the cursor gets an outline.

On export the target is converted into an [b]instruction line number[/b], so you never have to count lines yourself: comment lines ([code]#[/code]) and label lines
([code]label:[/code]) do not take up line numbers, which matches how the Mindustry assembler counts.
When the target block is deleted, references pointing at it are cleared in the same undo entry, so no dead references are left behind.